# Dark Sphere's ruling (CR 616.1, 616.1f): "If two or more of these effects would apply, you apply them sequentially." Bot2's
# Disintegrate for 5 aims at Bot1, who sacrifices both Spheres in response, choosing it each time. The first shield prevents
# 2 (half of 5, rounded down), the second half of the 3 left, rounded down: 1. Bot1 takes 2 (18). Halving the original 5
# twice would leave 1 (19); one shield only, 3 (17). Before the Disintegrate resolves, Bot2's Shock at Bot1 resolves while
# both shields wait: it is another source, so neither touches it and it is dealt in full (18) - a shield taking any source's
# damage would have prevented 1 of it (19) - and the Disintegrate then leaves Bot1 at 16.

